# Minimal bootable Saphira image, OpenRC target.
#
# Intentions ONLY. The package manager owns dependency closure; never
# enumerate resolved dependencies here (saphira-profiles(5)).
#
# The minimum for a genuinely bootable, manageable machine, and nothing
# more. Each entry earns its place:
#
#   saphira-base        libc/loader, filesystem layout, apk, shell, core
#                       runtime, account and package tooling. The one
#                       existing Saphira group; the profile layers onto it
#                       rather than re-enumerating it.
#   saphira-kernel      the kernel and its modules. Boot is impossible
#                       without it.
#   openrc              the init system for this target.
#   grub                the bootloader. Deliberately an explicit
#                       intention: a bootable image carries its own
#                       bootloader, and later kernel upgrades need it.
#   e2fsprogs           mkfs.ext4 for the root filesystem.
#   dosfstools          mkfs.vfat for the EFI System Partition. Required
#                       for any uefi-* target; harmless on bios-* (the
#                       creator refuses to use it there).
#   openssh             login/access. A server with no remote access is
#                       not manageable.
#   tzdata              a server with no timezone cannot reason about
#                       logs, certificates or scheduling.
#
# Deliberately absent, each a decision rather than an oversight:
#   - a graphical stack of any kind (see the headless policy);
#   - ca-certificates is already inside saphira-base;
#   - editors, mail, DNS, DHCP and web services: those are ROLE layers
#     (see the role-* profiles), not part of a minimal boot.
saphira-base
saphira-kernel
openrc
grub
e2fsprogs
dosfstools
openssh
tzdata
